Starbucks has reported positive same-store sales for the second quarter in a row as the long-term view of CEO Brian Niccol’s comeback plan comes into focus. The coffee chain saw a 4% increase in same-store sales both globally and in its North America division for the first quarter ended Dec. 28, driven mainly by transactions growth, which has been a challenge for the company in the past.&nbsp;

